module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smoothing.EssentiallySmoothEnlargement

/-!
# Absorbing a prescribed element into a coefficient-field enlargement

Let `b : D → T` be a flat local homomorphism of Artinian local rings whose target has nilpotent
maximal ideal, and assume the ideal identity `𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T`. The subring of `T` produced by
`Stacks.Smoothing.exists_essentiallySmooth_enlargement_residueField` — the image of
`D ⊗_{κ(D)} L` for a formally smooth extension `L` of the residue field of `D` — has residue
field exactly `L`, so an element `y ∈ T` whose residue lies in `L` agrees with an element of it
*modulo* `𝔪_T`. Turning that congruence into membership is the last step of Stacks 07FT, and this
file isolates its mechanism.

The mechanism is an `𝔪`-adic ladder. If `R ⊆ T` is a subring containing the image of `D`, then
`𝔪_T^j = 𝔪_D^j T` is generated over `T` by elements of `R`, so an element of `𝔪_T^j` is a
`T`-linear combination of elements of `R`; replacing each coefficient by a representative of its
residue class in `R` moves the element into `R + 𝔪_T^{j+1}`. Since `𝔪_T^n = 0` the ladder
terminates, and one obtains the main result:

a subring of `T` which contains the image of `D` and all of whose residue classes are
represented is **all** of `T`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Smoothing.exists_mem_sub_mem_pow_succ`: one rung of the ladder.
* `Stacks.Smoothing.eq_top_of_forall_exists_sub_mem_maximalIdeal`: the ladder, run to the top.
* `Stacks.Smoothing.eq_top_of_residue_surjective`: the same with the hypothesis read on residue
  fields.

## Implementation notes

*What this settles about Stacks 07FT, and what it does not.* In the situation of that tag
`D = k[y_1, …, y_m]_𝔭/𝔭^n`, `T = Λ_𝔮/𝔮^nΛ_𝔮` and the identity `𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T` is clause (1) of
Stacks 07FH (`Stacks.Smoothing.exists_mvPolynomial_flat_localization`), so the hypotheses below
are available. What the result says is that the subring `D'` wanted by clauses (2)–(3) cannot be
obtained by making its residue field large: a subring whose residues exhaust `κ(𝔮)` is the whole
of `T`, and `k[y]_𝔭/𝔭^n → Λ_𝔮/𝔮^nΛ_𝔮` is not essentially smooth in general — that is the content
of `Stacks.Smoothing.perfectClosure_le_of_isSeparableExtension`, which forbids `κ(𝔮)/κ(𝔭)` from
being separable. So the residue field `L` of `D'` is a *proper* subfield of `κ(𝔮)` and the
containment `E ⊆ D'` of clause (3) is a genuine condition on the coordinates of the elements of
`E`, not a consequence of their residues lying in `L`.

Concretely, the residual is this. Let `π_1, …, π_N ∈ 𝔪_D` generate `𝔪_D` and let `τ : L → T` be
the lift of `L ⊆ κ(𝔮)` supplied by formal smoothness. Applied to the subring generated by the
`b(π_i)` and the image of a ring-theoretic section `σ : κ(𝔮) → T` of the residue map — which
exists by Lemma 09EZ, `T` being Artinian local of characteristic `p` — the ladder below says
that subring is all of `T`, that is, every `y ∈ T` expands as `y = Σ_{|α| < n} σ(c_α) b(π)^α`
with `c_α ∈ κ(𝔮)`, the terms of degree `≥ n` vanishing. Such a `y` lies in the enlargement with
residue field `L` as soon as all `c_α ∈ L` and `σ` agrees with `τ` there. The open point
is the choice of the intermediate field: `L` must be separable over `κ(𝔭)` (that is what makes
`D → D'` essentially smooth with no power-taking), `κ(𝔭) = k(ȳ_1, …, ȳ_t)` is generated by the
residues of the first block of variables, and the coordinates `c_α` depend on `π` and `τ`, hence
on that very choice. Enlarging `L` to absorb new coordinates re-opens the expansion. This is the
same fixed-point problem that
`Stacks.Smoothing.exists_coefficientStage_basis_kaehlerDifferential` records for the source's own
route, now relocated from the λ-choice to the coordinates of `E`.

*Generality.* No characteristic hypothesis and no flatness of `b` is used below: the ladder is a
statement about a ring map `b : D → T` of local rings with `𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T` and `𝔪_T` nilpotent.
The hypothesis `hres` names the whole of what is needed about `R`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07FT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07FT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07FH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07FH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07FI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07FI)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing

namespace Stacks.Smoothing

variable {D T : Type*} [CommRing D] [CommRing T] [IsLocalRing D] [IsLocalRing T]

/-- **One rung of the `𝔪`-adic ladder.** Let `b : D → T` be a ring map of local rings with
`𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T`, and let `R` be a subring of `T` containing the image of `b` which meets every
residue class modulo `𝔪_T`. Then every element of `𝔪_T^j` agrees with an element of `R` modulo
`𝔪_T^{j+1}`.

The element is a `T`-linear combination of elements `b π` with `π ∈ 𝔪_D^j`, because
`𝔪_T^j = (𝔪_D T)^j` is generated by the image of `𝔪_D^j`; splitting each coefficient as an
element of `R` plus an element of `𝔪_T` puts the `R`-part in `R` and the rest in
`𝔪_T · 𝔪_T^j`. -/
theorem exists_mem_sub_mem_pow_succ (b : D →+* T) (R : Subring T) (hbR : ∀ d : D, b d ∈ R)
    (hmax : Ideal.map b (maximalIdeal D) = maximalIdeal T)
    (hres : ∀ y : T, ∃ r ∈ R, y - r ∈ maximalIdeal T) (j : ℕ) {y : T}
    (hy : y ∈ maximalIdeal T ^ j) :
    ∃ r ∈ R, y - r ∈ maximalIdeal T ^ (j + 1) := by
  have hpow : Ideal.map b (maximalIdeal D ^ j) = maximalIdeal T ^ j := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, hmax]
  rw [← hpow, Ideal.map] at hy
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨π, hπ, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact ⟨b π, hbR π, by simp⟩
  | zero => exact ⟨0, R.zero_mem, by simp⟩
  | add x z hx hz ihx ihz =>
    obtain ⟨rx, hrx, hx'⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨rz, hrz, hz'⟩ := ihz
    refine ⟨rx + rz, R.add_mem hrx hrz, ?_⟩
    have : x + z - (rx + rz) = (x - rx) + (z - rz) := by ring
    rw [this]
    exact Ideal.add_mem _ hx' hz'
  | smul a x hx ihx =>
    obtain ⟨rx, hrx, hx'⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨ra, hra, ha'⟩ := hres a
    have hxj : x ∈ maximalIdeal T ^ j := by rw [← hpow, Ideal.map]; exact hx
    refine ⟨ra * rx, R.mul_mem hra hrx, ?_⟩
    have hsplit : a • x - ra * rx = ra * (x - rx) + (a - ra) * x := by
      simp only [smul_eq_mul]; ring
    rw [hsplit]
    refine Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hx') ?_
    rw [pow_succ, mul_comm (maximalIdeal T ^ j)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul ha' hxj

/-- **The ladder, run to the top.** Let `b : D → T` be a ring map of local rings with
`𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T` and `𝔪_T^n = 0`, and let `R` be a subring of `T` containing the image of `b` which
meets every residue class modulo `𝔪_T`. Then `R = T`.

Added relative to the ambient situation of Stacks 07FT: nothing. The ideal identity is clause (1)
of Stacks 07FH, nilpotence of `𝔪_T` holds because `Λ_𝔮/𝔮^nΛ_𝔮` is Artinian local, and `hres` is
the hypothesis that the residues of `R` exhaust `κ(𝔮)`. -/
theorem eq_top_of_forall_exists_sub_mem_maximalIdeal (b : D →+* T) (R : Subring T)
    (hbR : ∀ d : D, b d ∈ R) (hmax : Ideal.map b (maximalIdeal D) = maximalIdeal T)
    (hres : ∀ y : T, ∃ r ∈ R, y - r ∈ maximalIdeal T) {n : ℕ}
    (hnil : maximalIdeal T ^ n = ⊥) : R = ⊤ := by
  have key : ∀ j : ℕ, ∀ y : T, ∃ r ∈ R, y - r ∈ maximalIdeal T ^ j := by
    intro j
    induction j with
    | zero => exact fun y => ⟨0, R.zero_mem, by simp⟩
    | succ j ih =>
      intro y
      obtain ⟨r, hrR, hr⟩ := ih y
      obtain ⟨r', hr'R, hr'⟩ :=
        exists_mem_sub_mem_pow_succ b R hbR hmax hres j hr
      refine ⟨r + r', R.add_mem hrR hr'R, ?_⟩
      have : y - (r + r') = y - r - r' := by ring
      rw [this]
      exact hr'
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun y _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨r, hrR, hr⟩ := key n y
  rw [hnil] at hr
  have : y - r = 0 := (Submodule.mem_bot T).mp hr
  rw [sub_eq_zero] at this
  exact this ▸ hrR

/-- **A subring whose residues exhaust the residue field is everything.** The previous result with
its hypothesis on `R` read on residue fields: for a ring map `b : D → T` of local rings with
`𝔪_T = 𝔪_D T` and `𝔪_T` nilpotent, a subring of `T` containing the image of `b` and surjecting
onto the residue field of `T` is the whole of `T`.

In the situation of Stacks 07FT this is the reason the subring `D` of clauses (2)–(3) must have a
*proper* residue field: were its residue field all of `κ(𝔮)` it would be `Λ_𝔮/𝔮^nΛ_𝔮` itself,
which is not essentially smooth over `k[y_1, …, y_m]_𝔭/𝔭^n` in general. -/
theorem eq_top_of_residue_surjective (b : D →+* T) (R : Subring T) (hbR : ∀ d : D, b d ∈ R)
    (hmax : Ideal.map b (maximalIdeal D) = maximalIdeal T) {n : ℕ}
    (hnil : maximalIdeal T ^ n = ⊥)
    (hsurj : ∀ c : ResidueField T, ∃ r ∈ R, residue T r = c) : R = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_of_forall_exists_sub_mem_maximalIdeal b R hbR hmax (fun y => ?_) hnil
  obtain ⟨r, hrR, hr⟩ := hsurj (residue T y)
  refine ⟨r, hrR, ?_⟩
  rw [← IsLocalRing.residue_eq_zero_iff, map_sub, hr, sub_self]

end Stacks.Smoothing

end
